    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "The distance from Davidson to Clare is $5\\frac{3}{10}$ km. A boy rides $2\\frac{3}{4}$ km from Davidson along the road to Clare. How much further does he have to ride to Clare?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$2\\frac{11}{20}$ km",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}5\\frac{3}{10}-2\\frac{3}{4}&=\\frac{53}{10}-\\frac{11}{4}\\\\5\\frac{3}{10}-2\\frac{3}{4}&=\\frac{106}{20}-\\frac{55}{20}\\\\5\\frac{3}{10}-2\\frac{3}{4}&=\\frac{51}{20}\\\\5\\frac{3}{10}-2\\frac{3}{4}&=2\\frac{11}{20}\\end{align*}$$\nHe has $2\\frac{11}{20}$ km further to ride.",
